        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Bukhara</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">500 BCE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">Officially in 500 BCE in the area now called the Ark, though the Bukhara oasis had been inhabited long before; in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shahnameh">Shahnameh</a> the city was founded by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siyavash">Siavash</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the Zeravshan River in south-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>, about 230 km west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a> trade centre; a Samanid capital and intellectual centre of the Islamic world; the birthplace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">Imam</a> Bukhari; the Kalan Minaret; the Karakhanid and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbeks">Uzbek</a> mosques and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">madrasas</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of Bukhara; the siege by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a> in 1220</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Bukhara is the capital of Bukhara Region in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>, and its historic centre is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</span></div>
